Vessim ↔ PyPSA dashboard
========================

This project re-implements, in Python, the numerical methods, the editable
spreadsheet interface and the single-line diagram conventions of two browser
tools by Adjie Brotot:

  * LoadFlow Simulator  — https://tool.adjiebrotots.com/loadflow-simulator/
  * ED-UC Simulator     — https://tool.adjiebrotots.com/ed-uc-simulator/

The original source, https://github.com/adjiebrotot/tool, is distributed under
the GNU General Public License v3.0.  No JavaScript from that repository is
copied here: the Newton-Raphson solver, the lambda-iteration economic dispatch,
the priority-list unit commitment, the table schemas, the SVG layout engine
(src/vessim_pypsa_dashboard/sld.py) and every device symbol were written from
scratch for this dashboard and are validated against PyPSA.  The tools are
credited as the source of the pedagogical design and of the visual vocabulary:
thick bus bars, orthogonal routes, flow arrows along each branch and the
results printed next to every element.

Third-party software used as dependencies (not vendored):

  * Vessim — dos-group, ML Systems Lab (Cambridge). MIT licence.
    https://github.com/dos-group/vessim
  * PyPSA — GPL-3.0.  Used as a library through its public Python API.
    https://github.com/PyPSA/PyPSA
  * HiGHS — MIT licence, through linopy / highspy.
  * Streamlit — Apache-2.0.   Plotly — MIT.

Datasets bundled under src/vessim_pypsa_dashboard/data/ come from the Vessim
repository (MIT) and are used unmodified.

This dashboard is an independent, academic add-on.  It is not affiliated with
or endorsed by the Vessim maintainers, PyPSA or Adjie Brotot.
